    {
      "id": "claim_b74e95c8922146189264a98cfbb86f54",
      "statement": "Opt-in debug file logging creates one active per-thread handler only after hardening the directory and file: POSIX uses owner-only permissions and no-follow opens, Windows replaces the file DACL with current-user access, unsafe thread IDs are hashed into filenames, and hardening failures disable tagged file handlers rather than risk an unsafe write.",
